  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Felix Wagner is terminated, so his seat can be reclaimed. Next step is getting the manager's approval.\n\nYou now have a DesignSuite license. Here's how it happened:\n\n- **No seats were free.** One seat was still assigned to someone who no longer works here, so I took it back and gave it to you.\n- **Approval:** Your manager, Ravi Shah, approved the license in our approval system.\n\nTry activating DesignSuite again. If it still says no seats are left, sign out of the app and back in to refresh it. If that doesn't fix it, message me. I've marked ticket T-6004 as resolved. Good luck with the onboarding redesign!"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Oh, great, thanks so much! I'll try activating it now. Quick question though, I wasn't sure who Felix Wagner is. Is that a coworker whose seat got reassigned? Just want to make sure I'm not taking something from someone who's still here."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're not taking anything from anyone who still works here. The seat you got belonged to someone who has left Quillmark. Our rules only let me take back a seat from someone who has left, or from a contractor whose contract has ended. Seats held by current employees are never touched, even ones away on leave.\n\nAnything else about that person's employment is a matter for HR or your manager, so I can't share more details. Your license is yours and it's legitimate. Let me know if activation gives you any trouble!"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks, that helps. I'll leave the rest of Felix's situation to HR or Ravi. I'm going to try activating DesignSuite now and I'll let you know if it gives me any trouble."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Sounds good! If activation gives you any trouble, message me here and I'll pick it back up. Enjoy the redesign work!"
  }
